/target/
# /results/* (not /results/) so the per-file exceptions below can actually
# re-include a file -- git cannot un-ignore a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY
# itself is excluded, only one whose directory is merely walked past.
/results/*
# Exceptions: cited as supporting evidence by committed report markdown
# (HALO_EXPLOIT_V*.md, REPORT_INDEX.ko.md, rust/SANDBOX_BOUNDARY.ko.md,
# artifacts/sandbox_benchmark/*.ko.md) -- tests/test_document_links.py checks
# every relative Markdown link resolves on disk, which only holds in CI if
# these two specific result files are actually tracked, not just present on
# whichever machine last ran the benchmark. The rest of /results/ (large,
# regenerable raw benchmark dumps) stays ignored.
!/results/attack-100-validated-20.json
!/results/attack-100-exec-fix.json
